/**
 * @defgroup StIstSimMaker IST Simulation Makers
 *
 * @brief Fast and slow Monte Carlo simulation of the STAR Intermediate Silicon
 *        Tracker (IST) silicon strip detector.
 *
 * @section ist_overview Overview
 *
 * The IST is a single-layer silicon strip detector positioned between the
 * Heavy Flavour Tracker (HFT) pixel detector and the Time Projection Chamber
 * (TPC).  It provides track-seeding and linking for charm-hadron reconstruction
 * by constraining track trajectories in the radial gap between those two
 * sub-detectors.
 *
 * @subsection ist_geometry Detector Geometry
 *
 * | Quantity                      | Value                    |
 * |-------------------------------|--------------------------|
 * | Ladders                       | 24                       |
 * | Sensors per ladder            | 6                        |
 * | Total sensors                 | 144                      |
 * | Rows per sensor (r-phi)       | 64                       |
 * | Columns per sensor (z)        | 12                       |
 * | Pads per sensor               | 768                      |
 * | Pad pitch (r-phi)             | 595.4 µm                 |
 * | Pad pitch (z)                 | 6275 µm                  |
 * | Active area (r-phi)           | 38.016 mm                |
 * | Active area (z)               | 75.30 mm                 |
 * | Sensor thickness              | 300 µm                   |
 * | Position resolution (r-phi)   | 163 µm (cluster size 1)  |
 * | Position resolution (z)       | 2325 µm                  |
 *
 * @subsection ist_electronics Electronics Chain
 *
 * Each sensor is read out by APV25 analogue pipeline chips (one chip per
 * 64 strips).  The analogue pipeline samples at the LHC bunch-crossing clock
 * frequency and stores up to 9 time-bin samples.  The stored samples are
 * multiplexed onto a 40 MHz output bus, digitised by a 12-bit ADC
 * (maximum value 4 096 counts), and zero-suppressed before being sent to the
 * data acquisition system via ARM-boards and RDOs.
 *
 * | Electronics level | Count per unit            | Total    |
 * |-------------------|---------------------------|----------|
 * | RDOs              | —                         | 6        |
 * | ARMs per RDO      | 6                         | 36       |
 * | APV25 per ARM     | 24                        | 864      |
 * | Channels per APV  | 128                       | 110 592  |
 * | APV25 per ladder  | 36 (12 per section × 3)   | 864      |
 *
 * @section ist_sim_comparison Fast vs. Slow Simulation
 *
 * Two makers are provided, trading physics fidelity against speed:
 *
 * @subsection ist_fast_sim Fast Simulation (StIstFastSimMaker)
 *
 * The fast simulator is designed for high-statistics productions where CPU
 * time is the dominant constraint.  It processes a single GEANT hit per
 * sensor crossing, applying one of two hit-position models:
 *
 * 1. **Gaussian smearing** (default): the GEANT hit position @f$ x_0 @f$ is
 *    replaced by a sample drawn from
 *    @f[
 *      x' \sim \mathcal{N}(x_0,\,\sigma)
 *    @f]
 *    where @f$\sigma@f$ is the position resolution loaded from the
 *    calibration database (@c ist1HitError table).  The sample is
 *    redrawn while @f$|x'| > L/2@f$ to stay within the active sensor
 *    half-length @f$L@f$.
 *
 * 2. **Pixelisation** (smearing disabled): the hit is snapped to the centre
 *    of the nearest pad.  Row and column indices are computed as
 *    @f[
 *      n_\text{row}    = \bigl\lfloor r_\phi / p_r \bigr\rfloor + 1, \qquad
 *      n_\text{col}    = \bigl\lfloor z    / p_z \bigr\rfloor + 1
 *    @f]
 *    where @f$p_r = 595.4\,\mu\text{m}@f$ and
 *    @f$p_z = 6275\,\mu\text{m}@f$ are the pad pitches.
 *
 * The local position (smeared or pixelised) is transformed to global
 * coordinates with a TGeoHMatrix taken from either the ideal VMC geometry or
 * the mis-alignment DB tables.  The energy deposit @f$\mathrm{d}E@f$ is
 * passed through unchanged (in GeV), and an StIstHit is added to
 * StIstHitCollection.
 *
 * @subsection ist_slow_sim Slow Simulation (StIstSlowSimMaker)
 *
 * The slow simulator models the full analogue signal chain and produces
 * @em raw ADC data in StIstCollection, which can be fed into the same
 * reconstruction chain as real detector data.  The main steps are:
 *
 * 1. **Hit-efficiency filtering** — Each MC hit is accepted with probability
 *    @f$\epsilon(p)@f$ according to the selected mode (see §@ref ist_hiteff).
 *
 * 2. **Track-segment reconstruction** — The GEANT mid-point position and local
 *    momentum direction are used to reconstruct the entry (@f$\mathbf{r}_\text{in}@f$)
 *    and exit (@f$\mathbf{r}_\text{out}@f$) points of the sensor crossing:
 *    @f[
 *      \mathbf{r}_\text{in}  = \mathbf{r}_\text{mid} - \hat{p}\,\Delta s/2, \qquad
 *      \mathbf{r}_\text{out} = \mathbf{r}_\text{mid} + \hat{p}\,\Delta s/2
 *    @f]
 *    where @f$\Delta s@f$ is the path length stored in the GEANT hit.
 *
 * 3. **Pad-crossing scan** — The track segment is walked pad-by-pad (in both
 *    r-phi and z simultaneously) using distanceToBorder() to locate each
 *    pad-edge crossing point.  This yields a list of boundary points
 *    @f$\{\mathbf{c}_0, \mathbf{c}_1, \ldots, \mathbf{c}_n\}@f$ with
 *    @f$\mathbf{c}_0 = \mathbf{r}_\text{in}@f$ and
 *    @f$\mathbf{c}_n = \mathbf{r}_\text{out}@f$.
 *
 * 4. **Charge deposition** — For each pad segment @f$i@f$ the charge deposited
 *    is proportional to the path-length fraction:
 *    @f[
 *      q_i = \mathrm{d}E \times \frac{|\mathbf{c}_{i+1}-\mathbf{c}_i|}{|\mathbf{r}_\text{out}-\mathbf{r}_\text{in}|}
 *    @f]
 *
 * 5. **Energy-to-ADC conversion** — The energy deposit is converted to ADC
 *    counts using a MIP-normalised scale factor:
 *    @f[
 *      k_\text{MPV} = \frac{A_\text{MIP}}{(dE/dx)_\text{Si} \cdot t}
 *                   = \frac{441}{3.87 \times 10^{-3}\,\text{GeV/cm}
 *                              \times 0.03\,\text{cm}}
 *                   \approx 3.80 \times 10^6\;\text{ADC counts/GeV}
 *    @f]
 *    where @f$A_\text{MIP} = 441@f$ ADC counts is the most-probable ADC
 *    value for a MIP, @f$(dE/dx)_\text{Si} = 3.87\,\text{MeV/cm}@f$, and
 *    @f$t = 300\,\mu\text{m}@f$ is the sensor thickness.
 *
 * 6. **APV25 time-bin response** — The ADC charge is distributed across the
 *    @f$N_\text{TB}@f$ time bins following a Landau-shaped pulse profile:
 *    @f[
 *      f_t = \frac{\int_{t-1/2}^{t+1/2} \mathcal{L}(u;\,\mu,\,\sigma)\,\mathrm{d}u}
 *                {\int_0^{N_\text{TB}} \mathcal{L}(u;\,\mu,\,\sigma)\,\mathrm{d}u}
 *    @f]
 *    with Landau peak @f$\mu = 3.8@f$ and width @f$\sigma = 1.168@f$ (in
 *    arbitrary time-bin units).  The ADC value in time bin @f$t@f$ is then
 *    @f[
 *      \mathrm{ADC}(t) = q_i \times k_\text{MPV} \times
 *                        \frac{f_t}{f_{t_\text{peak}}}
 *    @f]
 *
 * @subsection ist_hiteff Hit-Efficiency Modes
 *
 * Three efficiency modes are available (selected via the @c istSimPar DB table):
 *
 * | Mode | Description                                          |
 * |------|------------------------------------------------------|
 * | 0    | 100 % efficiency (ideal)                             |
 * | 1    | Linear momentum dependence: @f$\epsilon(p) = \max\!\bigl[\epsilon_0,\,1-(1-\epsilon_0)p/p_\text{cut}\bigr]@f$ |
 * | 2    | Flat efficiency @f$\epsilon_0@f$ for all tracks       |
 *
 * @section ist_coordinate_systems Coordinate Systems
 *
 * | Frame           | Origin                     | x-axis        | z-axis  |
 * |-----------------|----------------------------|---------------|---------|
 * | STAR global     | Interaction vertex         | towards east  | beam    |
 * | Sensor local    | Centre of sensor           | r-phi         | beam    |
 * | Sensor-frame    | Active-area corner (0,0)   | r-phi from 0  | z from 0|
 *
 * The transformation between sensor-local and sensor-frame coordinates used
 * internally by the slow simulator is:
 * @f[
 *   x_\text{sf} = L_{r\phi}/2 - x_\text{local}, \qquad
 *   z_\text{sf} = z_\text{local} + L_z/2
 * @f]
 *
 * @{
 */

// ============================================================
// File documentation blocks
// ============================================================

/**
 * @file StIstFastSimMaker.h
 * @brief Declaration of StIstFastSimMaker — fast IST hit simulator.
 *
 * Transforms GEANT Monte Carlo hits (StMcIstHit) into reconstructed IST hits
 * (StIstHit) via Gaussian position smearing or pad-centre pixelisation.
 * The energy deposit is passed through unchanged.
 *
 * @ingroup StIstSimMaker
 */

/**
 * @file StIstFastSimMaker.cxx
 * @brief Implementation of StIstFastSimMaker.
 *
 * Reads StMcIstHitCollection from StMcEvent, applies optional smearing, and
 * fills StIstHitCollection in StEvent.  Geometry is obtained from either
 * the TGeoManager ideal geometry (VMC) or the IST mis-alignment DB tables.
 *
 * @ingroup StIstSimMaker
 */

/**
 * @file StIstSlowSimMaker.h
 * @brief Declaration of StIstSlowSimMaker — slow IST raw-ADC simulator.
 *
 * Models the full analogue signal chain: track-segment tracing through the
 * silicon pad structure, charge-sharing between pads, energy-to-ADC
 * conversion with a Landau-shaped time-bin profile, and output as raw ADC
 * data in StIstCollection ready for standard reconstruction.
 *
 * @ingroup StIstSimMaker
 */

/**
 * @file StIstSlowSimMaker.cxx
 * @brief Implementation of StIstSlowSimMaker.
 *
 * Core algorithms: pad-boundary walking (checkPadCrossing, distanceToBorder),
 * pad identification in sensor-frame coordinates (findPad,
 * getMCHitRowAndColumn), and raw-ADC generation with APV25 time-bin
 * response (generateRawHits).
 *
 * @ingroup StIstSimMaker
 */


// ============================================================
// StIstFastSimMaker
// ============================================================

/**
 * @class StIstFastSimMaker
 * @ingroup StIstSimMaker
 *
 * @brief Fast IST hit simulator.
 *
 * Converts GEANT Monte Carlo hits (StMcIstHit, stored in local sensor
 * coordinates) into reconstructed IST hits (StIstHit in global coordinates)
 * suitable for tracking in StEvent.
 *
 * The simulator supports two position-response models:
 *
 * - **Gaussian smearing** (mSmear = true, default): each hit coordinate is
 *   independently smeared by a Gaussian with mean zero and sigma read from
 *   the calibration database (@c ist1HitError table).  Samples outside the
 *   physical sensor boundary are discarded and redrawn.
 *
 * - **Pixelisation** (mSmear = false): the hit is snapped to the geometric
 *   centre of the containing pad.
 *
 * The transformed local position is mapped to global coordinates with a
 * TGeoHMatrix provided by either the ideal VMC geometry (mBuildIdealGeom =
 * true) or the IST DB mis-alignment tables (default).
 *
 * ### Data members
 *
 * | Member             | Type        | Default       | Description                                             |
 * |--------------------|-------------|---------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
 * | mIstRot            | THashList*  | nullptr       | Hash list of per-module geometry rotation matrices      |
 * | mIstDb             | StIstDb*    | nullptr       | Handle to the IST conditions database object            |
 * | mBuildIdealGeom    | Bool_t      | kFALSE        | Use ideal VMC geometry when true; DB tables when false  |
 * | mRandom            | TRandom1    | seed 65539    | Random number generator for Gaussian smearing           |
 * | mResXIst1          | Double_t    | from DB       | Hit position resolution in r-phi direction (cm)         |
 * | mResZIst1          | Double_t    | from DB       | Hit position resolution in z direction (cm)             |
 * | mSmear             | Bool_t      | kTRUE         | Enable Gaussian smearing of hit positions               |
 */

/**
 * @fn StIstFastSimMaker::StIstFastSimMaker(const Char_t *name, bool useRandomSeed)
 * @brief Constructor.
 * @param name       %Maker name passed to StMaker base class (default: @c "istFastSim").
 * @param useRandomSeed If true, seeds TRandom1 from the system clock so each
 *                      job produces independent statistics.  If false (default),
 *                      uses fixed seed 65539 for reproducibility.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StIstFastSimMaker::Init()
 * @brief STAR framework Init hook — no-op beyond logging.
 * @return kStOk always.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StIstFastSimMaker::InitRun(Int_t runNo)
 * @brief Loads run-dependent calibration and geometry for a new run.
 *
 * Performs the following steps in order:
 * 1. If ideal geometry is requested, ensures TGeoManager is loaded
 *    (via @c GetDataBase("VmcGeometry")).
 * 2. Reads the @c ist1HitError calibration table and extracts the r-phi
 *    and z position resolutions as
 *    @f$ \sigma_{r\phi} = \sqrt{c_0} @f$,
 *    @f$ \sigma_z = \sqrt{c_3} @f$
 *    where @f$c_i@f$ are the elements of the @c coeff[] array.
 * 3. Retrieves the StIstDb pointer from the @c "ist_db" dataset.
 * 4. Reads the per-module rotation matrices into mIstRot.
 *
 * @param runNo  Run number (not used directly; passed by the STAR framework).
 * @return kStOk on success; kStErr if the DB is unavailable;
 *         kFatal / kStFatal if geometry or rotation matrices are missing.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StIstFastSimMaker::Make()
 * @brief Main event-processing method.
 *
 * Algorithm:
 * 1. Retrieves StEvent and StMcEvent from the input dataset chain.
 * 2. Obtains (or creates) an StIstHitCollection in StEvent.
 * 3. Loops over all StMcIstHit objects in the first IST layer.
 * 4. For each MC hit, computes the sensor module index
 *    @f$ m = 1000 + (\text{ladder}-1) \times N_\text{sensor} + \text{wafer} @f$
 *    and retrieves the corresponding TGeoHMatrix.
 * 5. Applies Gaussian smearing or pixelisation to the local position.
 * 6. Transforms the local position to global coordinates via
 *    @c TGeoHMatrix::LocalToMaster().
 * 7. Constructs an StIstHit and adds it to the collection.
 *
 * @return kStOK on success; kStWarn if input data structures are absent;
 *         kStFatal if the MC hit collection is null.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstFastSimMaker::buildIdealGeom(Bool_t isIdealGeom)
 * @brief Selects the geometry source used for local-to-global transformation.
 * @param isIdealGeom  kTRUE to use the ideal VMC TGeoManager geometry;
 *                     kFALSE (default) to use the mis-alignment DB tables.
 */

/**
 * @fn Double_t StIstFastSimMaker::distortHit(const Double_t x, const Double_t res, const Double_t detLength)
 * @brief Smears a hit coordinate with a Gaussian and constrains it within the sensor.
 *
 * Draws a sample @f$x' \sim \mathcal{N}(x, \sigma)@f$ until
 * @f$|x'| \leq L@f$, where @f$\sigma@f$ = @p res and @f$L@f$ = @p detLength.
 * If the input @p x already lies outside the sensor, no smearing is applied
 * and a warning is issued.
 *
 * @param x          True hit coordinate in the local sensor frame (cm).
 * @param res        Gaussian sigma — position resolution (cm).
 * @param detLength  Half-length of the active sensor dimension (cm).
 * @return Smeared hit coordinate within @f$[-L, +L]@f$ (cm).
 */


// ============================================================
// StIstSlowSimMaker
// ============================================================

/**
 * @class StIstSlowSimMaker
 * @ingroup StIstSimMaker
 *
 * @brief Slow IST raw-ADC simulator.
 *
 * Models the complete signal chain from a GEANT energy deposit to APV25
 * analogue output sampled in up to 9 time bins.  Output is a set of raw ADC
 * values in StIstCollection (key @c "istRawAdcSimu"), which is consumed by
 * the same reconstruction chain (StIstRawHitMaker → StIstClusterMaker →
 * StIstHitMaker) as real detector data.
 *
 * ### Processing pipeline per MC hit
 *
 * ```
 * StMcIstHit
 *    │
 *    ├─ Hit-efficiency filter (mHitEffMode)
 *    │
 *    ├─ Reconstruct entry/exit points from mid-point + momentum direction
 *    │
 *    ├─ checkPadCrossing() — walk track segment through pad grid
 *    │       ├─ transformToSensor()
 *    │       ├─ findPad()
 *    │       └─ distanceToBorder()
 *    │
 *    └─ generateRawHits() — for each sub-segment in a pad:
 *            ├─ Charge proportional to path-length fraction
 *            ├─ × kIstMPV  (energy → ADC scale)
 *            └─ × f_t / f_peak  (Landau time-bin profile)
 *                 → StIstRawHit::setCharge(adc, timeBin)
 * ```
 *
 * ### Data members
 *
 * | Member                | Type                | Default       | Description                                                      |
 * |-----------------------|---------------------|---------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
 * | mIstDb                | StIstDb*            | nullptr       | Handle to the IST conditions database                            |
 * | mBuildIdealGeom       | Bool_t              | kFALSE        | Request ideal VMC geometry                                       |
 * | mIstCollectionPtr     | StIstCollection*    | nullptr       | Output raw-hit collection (owned by white board)                 |
 * | fAdc                  | TF1*                | Landau(µ=3.8,σ=1.168) | APV25 analogue pulse-shape function (time-bin response)  |
 * | mDefaultTimeBin       | UChar_t             | 9             | Default number of time bins (from istControl DB table)           |
 * | mCurrentTimeBinNum    | UChar_t             | 9             | Active number of time bins for the current run                   |
 * | mMappingGeomVec       | vector<int>         | size 110592   | Geometry-ID to electronics-ID lookup table                       |
 * | mHitEffMode           | short               | 0             | Hit-efficiency mode (0 = ideal, 1 = p-dependent, 2 = flat)       |
 * | mMomCut               | float               | 0.0 (GeV/c)   | Momentum threshold for mode-1 efficiency rolloff                 |
 * | mHitEff               | float               | 1.0           | Asymptotic single-hit efficiency (mode 1) or flat value (mode 2) |
 * | mRndGen               | TRandom3*           | gRandom       | Random number generator (shared with ROOT)                       |
 */

/**
 * @fn StIstSlowSimMaker::StIstSlowSimMaker(const char *name)
 * @brief Constructor.
 *
 * Initialises all data members and creates the APV25 pulse-shape TF1:
 * @verbatim
 *   fAdc = new TF1("fAdc","landau",0,9)
 *   fAdc->SetParameters(1.14288, 3.8, 1.168)
 * @endverbatim
 * The parameters represent (amplitude, most-probable value in time-bin units,
 * Landau width).  The mapping geometry vector is resized to kIstNumElecIds
 * (110 592).
 *
 * @param name  %Maker name passed to StMaker (default: @c "istSlowSim").
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StIstSlowSimMaker::Init()
 * @brief Allocates and registers the output StIstCollection.
 *
 * Creates an StIstCollection and registers it on the STAR white board under
 * the key @c "istRawAdcSimu".  This collection is accessed by downstream
 * reconstruction makers.
 *
 * @return kStOk on success; kStErr if allocation fails.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StIstSlowSimMaker::InitRun(Int_t runNumber)
 * @brief Loads run-dependent conditions: control parameters, channel mapping, and efficiency.
 *
 * Performs these steps:
 * 1. Retrieves the StIstDb pointer from @c "ist_db".
 * 2. Reads @c istControl table: sets mDefaultTimeBin and mCurrentTimeBinNum.
 * 3. Reads @c istMapping table: fills mMappingGeomVec with the geometry-ID
 *    to electronics-ID correspondence for all 110 592 channels.
 * 4. Reads @c istSimPar table: sets mHitEffMode, mMomCut, mHitEff.
 *
 * @param runNumber  Run number (used by the STAR framework for DB query).
 * @return kStOk on success; kStErr if any DB table is unavailable.
 */

/**
 * @fn Int_t StIstSlowSimMaker::Make()
 * @brief Main event-processing method.
 *
 * For each event:
 * 1. Resets the time-bin count in mIstCollectionPtr.
 * 2. Loops over all MC IST hits in the first layer.
 * 3. Applies hit-efficiency filtering (see §@ref ist_hiteff).
 * 4. Calls getMCHitRowAndColumn() to find the primary pad.
 * 5. Calls generateRawHits() to distribute charge across pads and time bins.
 *
 * @return kStOK on success; kStWarn if StMcEvent is absent.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstSlowSimMaker::Clear(Option_t *opts)
 * @brief Per-event cleanup — clears the raw-hit collection for each ladder.
 *
 * Called automatically by the STAR framework between events.  Iterates over
 * all kIstNumLadders (24) raw-hit collections and calls Clear() on each,
 * then delegates to StMaker::Clear().
 *
 * @param opts  Option string forwarded to TObject::Clear() (may be empty).
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstSlowSimMaker::buildIdealGeom(const Bool_t isIdealGeom)
 * @brief Selects ideal VMC geometry instead of DB mis-alignment tables.
 * @param isIdealGeom kTRUE for ideal geometry; kFALSE (default) for DB tables.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstSlowSimMaker::getMCHitRowAndColumn(const StMcIstHit *istMChit, UShort_t &meanColumn, UShort_t &meanRow) const
 * @brief Converts a GEANT hit local position to the pad row and column indices.
 *
 * Uses the sensor-local coordinate system where the origin is at the sensor
 * centre.  The r-phi and z coordinates are shifted to place the corner at
 * the origin before dividing by the pad pitches:
 * @f[
 *   r_\phi = L_{r\phi}/2 - x_\text{local}, \qquad
 *   z      = z_\text{local} + L_z/2
 * @f]
 * @f[
 *   n_\text{row} = \bigl\lfloor r_\phi / p_r \bigr\rfloor + 1, \qquad
 *   n_\text{col} = \bigl\lfloor z / p_z \bigr\rfloor + 1
 * @f]
 * Row numbering: 1–64 in r-phi direction.
 * Column numbering: 1–12 in z direction.
 *
 * @param istMChit    Pointer to the GEANT IST hit (not null).
 * @param[out] meanColumn  Column index of the containing pad (1–12).
 * @param[out] meanRow     Row index of the containing pad (1–64).
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstSlowSimMaker::generateRawHits(const StMcIstHit *istMChit) const
 * @brief Core method: distributes charge from one GEANT hit across pads and time bins.
 *
 * **Step 1 — Track segment reconstruction.**
 * Entry and exit points are computed from the GEANT mid-point and momentum
 * direction, using the path-length @f$\Delta s@f$:
 * @f[
 *   \mathbf{r}_\text{in}  = \mathbf{r}_\text{mid} - \hat{p}\,\Delta s/2, \qquad
 *   \mathbf{r}_\text{out} = \mathbf{r}_\text{mid} + \hat{p}\,\Delta s/2
 * @f]
 * Both are transformed to sensor-frame coordinates via transformToSensor().
 *
 * **Step 2 — Pad crossing.**
 * checkPadCrossing() walks the segment from @f$\mathbf{r}_\text{in}@f$ to
 * @f$\mathbf{r}_\text{out}@f$, building a list of pad-boundary crossings.
 *
 * **Step 3 — Geometry-to-electronics ID mapping.**
 * For each pad segment, the geometry ID is computed as:
 * @f[
 *   \text{geoId} = (\ell-1) \times 128 \times 36
 *                 + (s-1) \times 12 \times 64
 *                 + (c-1) \times 64 + r
 * @f]
 * where @f$\ell@f$, @f$s@f$, @f$c@f$, @f$r@f$ are the ladder, sensor,
 * column, and row indices.  The electronics ID is looked up in
 * mMappingGeomVec.
 *
 * **Step 4 — Charge and ADC calculation.**
 * The energy deposited in each pad segment is:
 * @f[
 *   q_i = \mathrm{d}E \times \frac{\ell_i}{\ell_\text{tot}}
 * @f]
 * where @f$\ell_i@f$ is the path length through pad @f$i@f$ and
 * @f$\ell_\text{tot}@f$ is the total path length.
 * The ADC in time bin @f$t@f$ is:
 * @f[
 *   \text{ADC}_t = q_i \times k_\text{MPV} \times f_t / f_\text{peak}
 * @f]
 * where @f$k_\text{MPV} \approx 3.80 \times 10^6\,\text{ADC/GeV}@f$ is the
 * MIP normalisation factor, and @f$f_t@f$ is the Landau time-bin fraction.
 *
 * Accumulated ADC values are added to any existing charge on the channel
 * (to handle overlapping hits from multiple tracks).  The IdTruth is set to
 * the track that deposited the majority of the charge.
 *
 * @param istMChit  Pointer to the GEANT IST hit (not null).
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstSlowSimMaker::checkPadCrossing(const StThreeVectorD inPos, const StThreeVectorD outPos, StThreeVectorD mcLocalDir, Double_t dS, vector<StThreeVectorD> &cross_vec) const
 * @brief Builds a list of points where the particle track crosses pad boundaries.
 *
 * Starting from @p inPos, the method advances along the track direction one
 * pad edge at a time (using distanceToBorder()) until reaching the pad that
 * contains @p outPos.  At each step, findPad() determines which pad the next
 * point is in.
 *
 * If either @p inPos or @p outPos maps to column 65535 (invalid / outside
 * sensor), the method returns a list containing only the entry point.
 *
 * The sign of the x-component of @p mcLocalDir is flipped on entry because
 * the sensor-frame x-axis runs opposite to the sensor-local x-axis.
 *
 * @param inPos       Entry point in sensor-frame coordinates (cm).
 * @param outPos      Exit point in sensor-frame coordinates (cm).
 * @param mcLocalDir  Unit direction vector of the track in sensor-local frame.
 * @param dS          Path length through the sensitive volume (cm, unused
 *                    directly but preserved for context).
 * @param[out] cross_vec  Ordered list of pad-boundary crossing points, including
 *                        @p inPos as first element and @p outPos as last.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstSlowSimMaker::transformToSensor(StThreeVectorD &hitPos) const
 * @brief Transforms a point from sensor-local to sensor-frame coordinates.
 *
 * The sensor-local frame has its origin at the sensor centre, with the x-axis
 * in the r-phi direction and z-axis along the beam.  The sensor-frame has its
 * origin at the corner of the active area, with x increasing from 0 to
 * @f$L_{r\phi}@f$ and z increasing from 0 to @f$L_z@f$:
 * @f[
 *   x_\text{sf} = L_{r\phi}/2 - x_\text{local}, \qquad
 *   z_\text{sf} = z_\text{local} + L_z/2
 * @f]
 *
 * @param[in,out] hitPos  Position vector modified in-place.
 *                        On entry: sensor-local (cm, origin at centre).
 *                        On exit: sensor-frame (cm, origin at corner).
 */

/**
 * @fn Double_t StIstSlowSimMaker::distanceToBorder(const StThreeVectorD hitPos, const StThreeVectorD dir, const StThreeVectorD mean, StThreeVectorD &dist) const
 * @brief Computes the 3-D displacement from a point to the nearest pad boundary.
 *
 * Each pad is treated as a rectangular box with half-widths
 * @f$(p_r/2,\,0.015\,\text{cm},\,p_z/2)@f$ in sensor-frame coordinates
 * (@f$p_r@f$ = r-phi pitch, @f$p_z@f$ = z pitch).  The method finds the
 * boundary plane (yz-plane at @f$x_\text{border}@f$ or xy-plane at
 * @f$z_\text{border}@f$) that is first intersected along @p dir, and returns
 * the 3-D displacement to that intersection.
 *
 * If @f$|d_x| < 10^{-6}@f$, only the z-border is considered; if
 * @f$|d_z| < 10^{-6}@f$, only the x-border is considered.
 *
 * @param hitPos  Current position in sensor-frame coordinates (cm).
 * @param dir     Unit direction vector of the track.
 * @param mean    Centre of the current pad in sensor-frame coordinates (cm).
 * @param[out] dist  3-D displacement vector to the pad boundary (cm).
 * @return Magnitude of @p dist (cm).
 */

/**
 * @fn void StIstSlowSimMaker::findPad(const StThreeVectorD hitPos, UShort_t &column, UShort_t &row, Double_t &rPhiPos_mean, Double_t &zPos_mean) const
 * @brief Identifies the pad containing a given sensor-frame position.
 *
 * Divides the sensor-frame coordinates by the pad pitches and rounds down:
 * @f[
 *   n_\text{row}  = \bigl\lfloor x_\text{sf} / p_r \bigr\rfloor + 1
 *                   \quad \text{clamped to } [1,\,64], \\
 *   n_\text{col}  = \bigl\lfloor z_\text{sf} / p_z \bigr\rfloor + 1
 *                   \quad \text{clamped to } [1,\,12]
 * @f]
 * Positions outside the active area by more than half a pad pitch return
 * sentinel value 65535 in all output arguments.
 *
 * The pad-centre positions are returned for use as the @c mean argument of
 * distanceToBorder():
 * @f[
 *   \bar{x} = (n_\text{row}-1)\,p_r + p_r/2, \qquad
 *   \bar{z} = (n_\text{col}-1)\,p_z + p_z/2
 * @f]
 *
 * @param hitPos         Position in sensor-frame coordinates (cm, origin at corner).
 * @param[out] column    Column index (1–12); 65535 if out-of-bounds.
 * @param[out] row       Row index (1–64); 65535 if out-of-bounds.
 * @param[out] rPhiPos_mean  r-phi coordinate of pad centre (cm).
 * @param[out] zPos_mean     z coordinate of pad centre (cm).
 */

/**
 * @fn Double_t StIstSlowSimMaker::direction(const Double_t x) const
 * @brief Returns the sign of a scalar: +1, 0, or −1.
 * @param x  Input scalar.
 * @return @f$\text{sgn}(x) \in \{-1,\,0,\,+1\}@f$.
 */

/**
 * @fn Double_t StIstSlowSimMaker::scaleFromYvsX(const StThreeVectorD vec, const Double_t a) const
 * @brief Scales a displacement @p a in x to the corresponding y displacement.
 *
 * Given a direction vector @p vec, returns @f$a \cdot v_y / v_x@f$.
 * Issues a warning and returns 0 if @f$|v_x| < 10^{-6}@f$.
 *
 * @param vec  Direction vector (dimensionless or any consistent units).
 * @param a    Displacement in x (cm).
 * @return Corresponding displacement in y (cm).
 */

/**
 * @fn Double_t StIstSlowSimMaker::scaleFromYvsZ(const StThreeVectorD vec, const Double_t a) const
 * @brief Scales a displacement @p a in z to the corresponding y displacement.
 *
 * Returns @f$a \cdot v_y / v_z@f$.
 * Issues a warning and returns 0 if @f$|v_z| < 10^{-6}@f$.
 *
 * @param vec  Direction vector.
 * @param a    Displacement in z (cm).
 * @return Corresponding displacement in y (cm).
 */

/** @} */ // end defgroup StIstSimMaker
